# Benchmark artifacts #
#######################
# Models, their configurations and the string vocabulary are written together by
# scripts/generate_benchmark_models.py. A model is ~190 MB, so the whole directory
# is generated on demand rather than committed. See benchmark-data/README.md.
benchmark-data/generated/

# Bundles from scripts/benchmark/package.sh -- a build artifact of the working tree.
benchmark-data/dist/

# Client and server logs and the summary table a run leaves behind. The curated
# reports in benchmark-data/results/ are what is tracked; the output they were
# written from is not.
benchmark-data/results/raw/

# Runbooks and working notes for our own benchmark campaigns. These name accounts,
# regions, bucket names and instance types we happen to be using, which is operational
# detail rather than anything a reader of this repository needs. The reusable parts of a
# campaign belong in documentation/ and benchmark-data/results/ instead.
benchmark-data/private/

# Written by scripts/benchmark/bootstrap.sh on a benchmark instance: that host's
# ORT_DYLIB_PATH and provider, which are per-host and not the repository's business.
/env.sh

# Rust build output #
#####################
/target/
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Python, for scripts/ #
########################
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Environment files, potentially sensitive #
###########################################
.env
.env.*

# OS-specific files #
#####################

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

